From bc167c581e734ae553cdaa4260ddd96274efea66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 12:22:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] pmb.build: give every chroot its own sccache server

sccache listens on 127.0.0.1:4226 by default. Every chroot of every
pmbootstrap work dir in the same network namespace therefore shares one
server: whichever build starts it first owns it, and a Rust build in
another chroot or work dir sends its compiles there. The server runs rustc
from its own root, so every crate fails with "sccache: caused by: No such
file or directory (os error 2)". Seen with two work dirs in one container:
a crossdirect mesa build in one broke a cross-native2 Rust build in the
other for as long as the first server lived.

Put the server on a Unix socket in the chroot's own /tmp
(SCCACHE_SERVER_UDS=/tmp/sccache.sock) for every build: the native chroot
for native and cross-native2 builds (RUSTC_WRAPPER), the foreign chroot
for crossdirect, whose rustc wrapper runs sccache with the inherited
environment.

kill_sccache() probed the TCP port and stopped "the" server from the
native chroot, which could be another work dir's. Stop each chroot's
server through its socket instead, with the sccache of that chroot, or
the native one mounted in a foreign chroot, and remove the socket.

Assisted-by: Claude
